[1mWhat the program turned out to be:[22m it reads one int with [38;5;10mscanf("%d")[0m, packs it into [38;5;10m{int, int, double}[0m = [38;5;10m{x, 3, 2.0}[0m, and hex-dumps the 16 struct bytes. No padding on x86-64, so output is always exactly 33 bytes. [38;5;10mscanf[0m's return value is never checked and [38;5;10mmain[0m always [38;5;10mreturn 0[0m, so there is no path where stderr is non-empty or the exit code is non-zero — I verified that empirically, including with stdin unreadable and stdout closed, rather than inferring it.[0m[0m
